---
title: Andrew Lum — welcome
description: Andrew Lum builds software, and the teams that build it. Engineering leader in Brooklyn, New York. Come in, sit down.
# Drop a headshot in src/img/ and set the filename here to show it, e.g.
# photo: /img/andrew.jpg
photo:
tended: November 2026
---

<div class="wrapper">

  <main>
    <section class="hello">
      {# Letterhead. The sprig holds the spot until there's a photo to put there. #}
      {% if photo %}
        <img class="portrait" src="{{ photo }}" alt="Andrew Lum" width="128" height="128">
      {% else %}
        {% include "sprig.njk" %}
      {% endif %}
      <h1 class="hi">
        Hi, I'm Andrew
        <span class="wave" role="img" aria-label="waving hand">👋</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        I build software, and the teams that build it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most recently I was Director of Engineering at Findigs, where I led
        product engineering on a platform that made renting an apartment faster
        and fairer. I left at the end of August 2026 to build again. Right now
        that means <a href="https://satsuma.works">Studio Satsuma</a>, a small
        studio for the apps I've wanted to exist. I'm always glad to talk about
        engineering leadership roles.
      </p>
      <p>
        I don't think leading and building are different jobs. A team is a
        system too. It has interfaces, feedback loops, and failure modes, and it
        gets better the same way software does: someone who cares pays attention
        to the details. I like the messy stuff, messy data and messy operations.
        And what someone writes down is rarely what they actually need; there's
        usually a frustration underneath that never made it into the ticket.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of work, I love to move. You'll usually find me climbing,
        cooking, running, dancing, or practicing handstands in the park. Most
        of the time, in Brooklyn.
      </p>
    </section>

    {% if collections.fieldnotes.length %}
    <section>
      <h2 class="label">Field Notes · notes on technical leadership</h2>
      <ul class="notes">
        {%- for note in collections.fieldnotes.slice(0, 5) %}
        <li><a href="{{ note.url }}">{{ note.data.title }}</a></li>
        {%- endfor %}
        <li class="more"><a href="/field-notes/">All notes →</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    <section>
      <h2 class="label">If you'd like to know more</h2>
      <ul class="links">
        <li>
          <a href="https://satsuma.works">Studio Satsuma</a>
          <span class="note">the studio where I build and ship small apps</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://andlum.com/sik-fan-lah/">Sik Fan Lah</a>
          <span class="note">dinner party menus, and the recipes behind them</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/andlum">GitHub</a>
          <span class="note">side projects, in varying states of repair</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/andlum">LinkedIn</a>
          <span class="note">the professional-shaped version of me, with the full work history. The best place to reach me.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>
      Last tended {{ tended }}<br>
      No analytics, no cookies, nothing following you out the door.
    </p>
  </footer>

</div>
